1
00:00:05,375 --> 00:00:10,225
Last time, we opened four crates: plants, animals, fungi and bacteria.

2
00:00:10,455 --> 00:00:13,855
Now we are back in our community garden, with the plants crate.

3
00:00:18,262 --> 00:00:19,442
Lock in first.

4
00:00:19,662 --> 00:00:21,082
And find the new lizard!

5
00:00:21,583 --> 00:00:26,783
Plants can be classified into two groups: flowering plants and non-flowering plants.

6
00:00:28,442 --> 00:00:30,782
This chilli plant has no flowers today.

7
00:00:30,872 --> 00:00:32,902
So it is a non-flowering plant!

8
00:00:33,032 --> 00:00:33,902
Round one.

9
00:00:34,162 --> 00:00:35,322
Is Momo right?

10
00:00:35,542 --> 00:00:36,902
No flowers today.

11
00:00:37,122 --> 00:00:39,772
Only green chillies, with seeds inside.

12
00:00:40,012 --> 00:00:41,852
One, it is a flowering plant.

13
00:00:42,072 --> 00:00:44,182
Two, it is a non-flowering plant.

14
00:00:44,402 --> 00:00:45,822
Show me with your fingers.

15
00:00:51,293 --> 00:00:52,243
Locked in!

16
00:00:52,373 --> 00:00:52,953
One!

17
00:00:53,113 --> 00:00:54,553
One is my lucky number.

18
00:00:54,603 --> 00:00:55,153
One.

19
00:00:55,533 --> 00:00:57,013
A chilli is a fruit.

20
00:00:57,263 --> 00:00:59,193
And fruits come from flowers.

21
00:00:59,766 --> 00:01:01,296
Watch this chilli plant.

22
00:01:01,516 --> 00:01:02,496
Speeded up.

23
00:01:03,804 --> 00:01:05,254
A small white flower.

24
00:01:05,924 --> 00:01:07,114
The petals drop.

25
00:01:07,824 --> 00:01:10,534
A tiny green chilli grows where the flower was.

26
00:01:11,656 --> 00:01:12,916
The answer is one.

27
00:01:13,136 --> 00:01:15,126
The flower developed into a fruit.

28
00:01:15,356 --> 00:01:17,406
And inside the fruit: seeds.

29
00:01:17,912 --> 00:01:20,222
A lucky number is not a reason, Basil.

30
00:01:20,452 --> 00:01:21,452
No point!

31
00:01:21,575 --> 00:01:22,545
One finger?

32
00:01:22,815 --> 00:01:23,955
One finger up!

33
00:01:24,532 --> 00:01:25,732
Say it with me!

34
00:01:26,438 --> 00:01:28,328
Flowering plants bear flowers.

35
00:01:28,558 --> 00:01:30,228
They reproduce from seeds.

36
00:01:30,438 --> 00:01:33,518
The flowers in flowering plants develop into fruits.

37
00:01:33,728 --> 00:01:35,538
The seeds are found in the fruits.

38
00:01:39,572 --> 00:01:40,592
And this one?

39
00:01:40,752 --> 00:01:41,762
No flowers.

40
00:01:41,942 --> 00:01:43,092
No fruits.

41
00:01:43,214 --> 00:01:45,214
That is a bird's nest fern, Momo.

42
00:01:45,464 --> 00:01:46,854
It never has flowers.

43
00:01:47,064 --> 00:01:48,754
So how does it make new plants?

44
00:01:48,974 --> 00:01:50,224
Look under a leaf.

45
00:01:50,454 --> 00:01:51,424
Shrink down.

46
00:01:51,654 --> 00:01:52,524
Quietly.

47
00:01:55,112 --> 00:01:56,392
You are tiny now.

48
00:01:56,722 --> 00:01:58,352
You are under a fern leaf.

49
00:01:59,177 --> 00:02:02,057
Above you: brown spore bags, in neat rows.

50
00:02:03,182 --> 00:02:04,512
One bag opens.

51
00:02:05,637 --> 00:02:07,027
Out come the spores.

52
00:02:07,347 --> 00:02:08,757
As fine as dust.

53
00:02:09,087 --> 00:02:10,507
And you are one of them.

54
00:02:11,220 --> 00:02:12,920
The wind carries you away.

55
00:02:14,835 --> 00:02:16,365
You land on damp soil.

56
00:02:17,689 --> 00:02:19,899
In time, a new fern grows here.

57
00:02:23,007 --> 00:02:24,147
No flowers.

58
00:02:24,377 --> 00:02:25,417
No seeds.

59
00:02:25,647 --> 00:02:29,127
A fern reproduces from spores, kept in spore bags.

60
00:02:31,537 --> 00:02:32,747
Say it with me!

61
00:02:33,461 --> 00:02:35,951
Non-flowering plants do not bear flowers.

62
00:02:36,171 --> 00:02:39,701
They reproduce from spores that may be found in spore bags.

63
00:02:43,736 --> 00:02:44,556
Spores?

64
00:02:44,636 --> 00:02:46,196
Mushrooms have spores too!

65
00:02:46,286 --> 00:02:47,756
So a fern is a fungus?

66
00:02:47,886 --> 00:02:49,256
Good thinking, Basil.

67
00:02:49,466 --> 00:02:52,206
But a fern makes its own food when there is light.

68
00:02:52,436 --> 00:02:53,646
So it is a plant.

69
00:02:55,148 --> 00:02:56,558
My plant notes!

70
00:02:56,683 --> 00:02:57,243
One.

71
00:02:57,613 --> 00:02:59,573
Hibiscus: a flowering plant.

72
00:02:59,903 --> 00:03:00,643
Two.

73
00:03:00,713 --> 00:03:03,503
Bird's nest fern: a non-flowering plant.

74
00:03:03,643 --> 00:03:04,553
Three.

75
00:03:04,703 --> 00:03:06,833
Grass: a non-flowering plant.

76
00:03:07,182 --> 00:03:08,062
Showdown!

77
00:03:08,302 --> 00:03:09,392
Double points.

78
00:03:09,632 --> 00:03:11,212
One line has a mistake.

79
00:03:11,442 --> 00:03:13,152
Line one, two, or three?

80
00:03:13,382 --> 00:03:14,792
Show me with your fingers.

81
00:03:21,260 --> 00:03:22,210
Locked in!

82
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:23,030
Three!

83
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:24,590
I hide in long grass.

84
00:03:24,630 --> 00:03:26,440
It has tiny flowers on top.

85
00:03:26,495 --> 00:03:27,325
Three!

86
00:03:27,435 --> 00:03:28,475
Me too.

87
00:03:28,526 --> 00:03:29,106
Oops!

88
00:03:29,990 --> 00:03:31,680
Grass is a flowering plant.

89
00:03:31,890 --> 00:03:33,290
Its flowers are tiny.

90
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:36,560
The grass-cutter usually cuts them off before we see them.

91
00:03:36,694 --> 00:03:37,324
Fixed!

92
00:03:37,674 --> 00:03:39,504
Grass: a flowering plant.

93
00:03:39,628 --> 00:03:40,958
Showed three fingers?

94
00:03:41,148 --> 00:03:43,048
Put up two more on your score hand!

95
00:03:43,549 --> 00:03:45,689
Plants are one of the four main groups.

96
00:03:45,919 --> 00:03:47,279
Remember all four?

97
00:03:47,643 --> 00:03:48,704
Say it with us!

98
00:03:49,364 --> 00:03:50,034
Plants!

99
00:03:49,839 --> 00:03:50,559
Animals!

100
00:03:50,314 --> 00:03:51,014
Fungi!

101
00:03:50,789 --> 00:03:51,659
Bacteria!

102
00:03:53,164 --> 00:03:54,914
Four main groups of living things!

103
00:03:56,964 --> 00:03:57,634
Plants!

104
00:03:57,439 --> 00:03:58,159
Animals!

105
00:03:57,914 --> 00:03:58,614
Fungi!

106
00:03:58,389 --> 00:03:59,259
Bacteria!

107
00:03:58,864 --> 00:04:00,614
Four main groups of living things!

108
00:04:01,719 --> 00:04:03,109
Show me your score hand!

109
00:04:03,339 --> 00:04:04,349
More than two?

110
00:04:04,579 --> 00:04:05,859
You beat the Buddies.

111
00:04:06,079 --> 00:04:07,139
Three fingers?

112
00:04:07,359 --> 00:04:08,359
High five!

113
00:04:08,856 --> 00:04:10,216
Did you spot the lizard?

114
00:04:10,466 --> 00:04:12,616
It was on the tree trunk, under the fern.

115
00:04:12,816 --> 00:04:15,666
Does a new lizard come from a seed, a spore, or an

116
00:04:15,416 --> 00:04:15,956
egg?

117
00:04:16,176 --> 00:04:17,456
Tell someone at home.

118
00:04:17,957 --> 00:04:18,867
Your turn.

119
00:04:19,097 --> 00:04:23,207
Find one flowering plant and one non-flowering plant near your home.

120
00:04:23,447 --> 00:04:24,107
Look.

121
00:04:24,377 --> 00:04:25,377
Do not pick.

122
00:04:26,158 --> 00:04:27,848
Next time: animals!

123
00:04:28,078 --> 00:04:28,908
A frog.

124
00:04:29,168 --> 00:04:29,968
A bird.

125
00:04:30,228 --> 00:04:31,078
A fish.

126
00:04:31,298 --> 00:04:33,248
Feathers, scales, or moist skin?

127
00:04:33,478 --> 00:04:35,368
Lock in your answer for next time.

128
00:04:36,089 --> 00:04:38,249
Let's read today's key words together!

129
00:04:38,489 --> 00:04:39,209
Ready?

130
00:04:39,499 --> 00:04:40,739
Flowering plants.

131
00:04:42,371 --> 00:04:43,461
Spore bags.

132
00:04:44,959 --> 00:04:46,399
Non-flowering plants.

133
00:04:48,266 --> 00:04:49,166
Well done!

134
00:04:50,149 --> 00:04:51,210
Say it with us!

135
00:04:52,010 --> 00:04:52,720
Ready?

136
00:04:52,844 --> 00:04:53,464
One!

137
00:04:53,844 --> 00:04:54,524
two!

138
00:04:54,849 --> 00:04:56,024
Now you know!
